It is essential to highlight that our evaluation methodology involves computing the mean CER and WER across samples in the test dataset. Alternatively, a common approach is to calculate the weighted average based on sample length. This helps to reduce length-related bias and typically yields smaller metric values, but can be subject to misinterpretation as it does not reflect the mean value of the metric across the entire test dataset. Hence, we opted not to employ this approach and instead computed the unweighted average of CER/WER.

